#
# The commit of 1bit-MONSTER/llama.cpp `1bit/hrx-vulkan` (our mirror of AMD's HRX line) that the daily
# bump-hrx run must not move away from. While a commit is named here, bump-hrx does not move the mirror,
# does not merge AMD's llama.cpp pin into `1bit/hrx-vulkan-patched`, reports the hold in the run summary and
# succeeds. Delete the commit line to lift the hold.
#
# The hold is for one situation only: AMD rewrote its line, so its pin no longer descends from the mirror,
# and taking it is a hand merge that has not been done yet. The run FAILS, naming this file, when the file
# is out of date (the mirror is no longer the named commit) or no longer needed (AMD's pin contains the
# named commit again), so a hold cannot outlive the state it describes.
#
# HELD 2026-11-11 for the release (orchestrator decision on engine#1945, the owner having delegated technical
# calls): the engine's llama.cpp pin stays where it is, and the merge of AMD's rebased line is post-release work.
# The state this records:
#   mirror  1bit/hrx-vulkan           44ee5710d19f7f3af79b99bbcbe5fd13979d1f67   (AMD's line before its rebase)
#   AMD pin                           9bf5871310a8d7de74f4cb0c57009835fbf91c27   (the rebased line, 1777 upstream commits newer)
#   merge into 1bit/hrx-vulkan-patched, against the last AMD commit our line took (43b0ec2c41cc):
#                                     149 conflicted files, 538 hunks (65 files / 83 hunks in the HRX backend)
# Lift it by deleting the line below, once AMD's line has been merged into ours.
44ee5710d19f7f3af79b99bbcbe5fd13979d1f67
